      ],
      "impact": "If C14 is in series with D2, the LED will not conduct DC and the heater-on indication will be dead; if C14 is in parallel, the LED has no current limit and may be overdriven. Either way the intended visual heater indicator does not function as specified.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic largely matches the specified architecture, but the heater status indicator on the Microcontroller sheet is built with LED D2 and a 22 µF capacitor C14 instead of the specified D2 plus series resistor R3, so the heater-on visual indicator is not implemented as intended."
